  "worked_solution": "The coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(-1).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{\u2033}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ {f}^{\u2034}(x) & =-\\frac{24}{{x}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{\u2034}(-1),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2034}(-1)=-\\frac{24}{(-1)^{5}}=-\\frac{24}{(-1)}=24.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{\u2034}(-1)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot 24=\\frac{24}{6}=4.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ is $4.$",
